((cmavo)) which are officially unassigned, excluding ((experimental cmavo)).

*((bi'a))
*((bo'a))
*((bo'e))
*((bo'i))
*((bo'o))
*((bo'u))
*((ci'a))
*((ja'u))
*((ne'e))
*((te'i))
*((zi'a))
*((zi'i))
*((zi'u))

bo'X is the only series of a-e-i-o-u left, and zi'X is the only series of i-a-u left, so they shouldn't be touched without very good reason.

* ((po'a)) is included in the 1994 version of cmavo list, but not in the 1998 one. Is it assigned or not? --((Cyril Slobin|kir))
**What was it assigned to? And is there any other current cmavo that has po'a's function? (--((And)))
***In elder version of the cmavo list, pe'a..po'a was an open/close pair for figurative speech. In newer version, pe'a become UI, and po'a gone. --((Cyril Slobin|kir))

